facts.claim:
`bin/local-dev.sh up` does the following:
- brings up docker infra (project texera-local-dev: postgres, rustfs, lakefs, lakekeeper(+migrate/init), litellm, jupyter) from bin/single-node/docker-compose.yml plus an overlay that publishes 5432/8000/8181/4000;
- bootstraps the DDL and replays liquibase updates;
- runs `sbt <proj>/dist` and unzips the results;
- starts these natively: config 9094, access-control 9096, file 9092, compiling 9090, CU-managing (app 8888; the script probes admin port 8082), notebook-migration 9098, texera-web 8080 and computing-unit-master 8085 (both from the amber dist, cwd amber), agent-service 3001 (`bun run dev`), frontend 4200.

local-dev exports:
- STORAGE_S3_ENDPOINT=http://<host LAN IP>:9000 (fatal if no LAN IP);
- JDBC texera/password@localhost:5432;
- Iceberg REST http://localhost:8181/catalog;
- USER_SYS_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=false.
State and logs live in /tmp/texera-local-dev (logs/<svc>.log). It refuses to start infra if 5432/9000/8000/8181/4000 are held by other containers. AGENTS.md: only one local-dev stack per machine.

Every k8s unit receives:
- STORAGE_JDBC url, user and password;
- S3 endpoint and keys;
- the lakeFS endpoint;
- the Iceberg catalog type, REST uri and warehouse name;
- file-service presign/upload URLs;
- AUTH_JWT_SECRET (required, 503 if unset);
- the creator's JWT as USER_JWT_TOKEN;
- JAVA_OPTS.
STORAGE_WAREHOUSE_ENABLED is not forwarded.

A run needs:
- a persisted workflow (vid = its latest version);
- an existing workflow_computing_unit row (FK cuid);
- a uid from the token;
- with storage.warehouse.enabled=true (default) and the rest catalog (default): a warehouseId owned by the caller. Otherwise it fails with 'a warehouse must be selected for this execution'.
The postgres catalog turns warehouses off, and then a warehouseId is rejected.

